      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Hi Stuart, the right way is format=xml, for the REST API.  The documentation page for that, at<br/>\n<a href=\"http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCR30/REST+API\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCR30/REST+API</a><br/>\n...was incorrect in stating that xml=true works.  I just fixed that.</p>\n\n<p>The old way, done for \"API-A-Lite\" (which we're trying to move away from) was xml=true.  The old way won't be changed in favor of steering people to use the REST API, which does it consistently.</p>\n\n<p>Thanks,<br/>\nChris</p>",
     "created": "18/May/10 2:07 PM",
